---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Fact-checking & editorial policy">
  <article
    class="article-wrap prose"
    style="margin-top:45px;margin-bottom:55px"
  >
    <span class="eyebrow">Trust & transparency</span>
    <h1>Fact-checking & editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: 10 September 2026</p>
    <h2>Original work and clear sourcing</h2>
    <p>
      We publish original writing. News must have a named author, publication
      date, category, relevant licensed image and a direct source link.
      Reporting should favour primary sources and distinguish verified facts,
      personal experience and opinion.
    </p>
    <h2>Rules can change</h2>
    <p>
      Legal, immigration, tax, visa and property information may change and may
      depend on individual circumstances. Relevant guides include a visible
      review date, official sources and a clear statement that general
      information does not replace advice from a qualified professional. Readers
      should verify important details with the competent Croatian authority
      before acting.
    </p>
    <h2>Personal stories and interviews</h2>
    <p>
      We do not invent people, interviews, quotes, testimonials or personal
      experiences. Participants’ names, biographies and quotations must be
      checked. Portraits and recordings require appropriate permission. One
      person’s application outcome is not evidence of another person’s
      eligibility.
    </p>
    <h2>Samples and unfinished reporting</h2>
    <p>
      Sample articles and templates are visibly labelled and excluded from
      search indexing and RSS. City research frameworks are not presented as
      completed local reporting. Samples must be reviewed and rewritten where
      necessary before their sample label is removed.
    </p>
    <h2>Images and videos</h2>
    <p>
      Images must have documented permission or a suitable licence, with creator
      and source credits. We do not use AI-generated images to represent factual
      news, real interview participants or documentary events. Videos only enter
      the site through the manually approved list.
    </p>
    <h2>Prices, statistics and dates</h2>
    <p>
      Current figures require a source, date and useful context. Asking prices
      are not presented as completed sale values. We do not create popularity
      figures or audience statistics before evidence exists.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Submit the page, the disputed detail and a reliable source through{' '}
      <a href={href('contact/?type=Correction')}>Contact & submissions</a> when
      open. Material corrections should be noted on the article with a date and
      explanation, while updated guides receive an updated date.
    </p>
    <h2>Commercial relationships</h2>
    <p>
      Sponsorships, advertising and affiliate links must be clearly disclosed. A
      commercial relationship does not remove the need to verify claims or
      correct errors. We do not publish fake testimonials.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
